hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20606","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, al-Mushma'ill narrated to us, Amr ibn Sulaym al-Muzani narrated to me that he heard Rafi' ibn Amr al-Muzani say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, while I was a young servant: Al-Ajwah and the tree are from Paradise."
"20607","Bahz and Abu al-Nadr and Affan narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me among my ummah there will be a people who recite the Qur'an not passing their throats, they will exit the religion as the arrow exits the game, then they will never return to it, the evilest of creation and creatures."
"20608","Ibn al-Samit said: So I met Rafi', Bahz said: the brother of al-Hakam ibn Amr, and I told him this hadith. He said: And I also heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20609","Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi al-Hakam al-Ghifari say: My grandmother narrated to me, from her father's uncle Rafi' ibn Amr al-Ghifari, he said: When I was a boy I used to pelt the date-palms of the Ansar. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought news and it was said: Here is a boy pelting our palms. So I was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O boy, why do you pelt the palms? He said: I said: I eat. He said: Do not pelt the palms, and eat what falls beneath them. Then he wiped my head and said: O Allah, fill his belly."
"20610","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Mushma'ill ibn Amr al-Muzani narrated to us, Amr ibn Sulaym al-Muzani narrated to us, from Rafi' ibn Amr al-Muzani, he says, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Al-Ajwah and the rock, or he said: Al-Ajwah and the tree, is in Paradise, al-Mushma'ill doubted."
"20611","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, al-Mushma'ill ibn Iyas narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Sulaym say: I heard Rafi' ibn Amr al-Muzani say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Al-Ajwah and the rock are from Paradise."
"20612","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Samit narrated to us, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me among my ummah there will be a people who recite the Qur'an not passing their throats, they will exit the religion as the arrow exits the game, then they will never return to it, the evilest of creation and creatures."
"20613","Ibn al-Samit said: So I met Rafi' and told him, and he said: And I also heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
